    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "German media across the spectrum repeatedly stress that the rapid spread of AI and large‑language models is outpacing existing data‑protection and cybersecurity safeguards, prompting calls for stronger oversight and a faster rollout of the EU AI Act. At the same time they agree that German companies are still lagging in practical AI adoption, especially in recruiting and operational processes, which fuels a consensus that substantial public investment in broadband, digital skills and education is essential to avoid a competitiveness gap. Finally, despite divergent political tones, the coverage converges on the view that automation will reshape the labour market and that coordinated policy measures are needed to mitigate job displacement while harnessing AI’s growth potential.",
